// Verified drill library, batch 1 (Nov 2026).
// Every drill below is taken from a named, publicly available source and
// rewritten in our own words with an original diagram. Rules followed:
//   - nothing added that the source doesn't say; gaps are stated in `srcnote`;
//   - distances are given as the source gives them (usually yards);
//     diagrams are drawn in metres (1 yd ≈ 0.91 m) and are schematic where
//     the source gives no spacing;
//   - `level` is only set when the source states it (levelSrc says where);
//   - labels: H = handler/thrower, C = cutter/receiver, D = defender, M = marker.
// Diagram key: blue = offence, red = defence, yellow = disc, solid = run,
// dashed = throw, dotted = optional run.

